<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="NEH" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Nehemiah</para>
  <para style="mt">Nehemiah</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The words of Nechemyah <char style="add">[God comforts]</char> the son of Hakhalyah <char style="add">[whom Yehovah enlightens]</char>. And it came to pass in the month Kislev <char style="add">[his confidence]</char>, in the twentieth year, as I was in Shushan <char style="add">[lily]</char> the palace,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />That Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char>, one of my brethren, came, he and <char style="add">[certain]</char> men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; and I asked them concerning the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char> that had escaped, which were left of the captivity, and concerning Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they said unto me, The remnant that are left of the captivity there in the province <char style="add">[are]</char> in great affliction and reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char>: the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> also <char style="add">[is]</char> broken down, and the gates thereof are burned with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass, when I heard these words, that I sat down and wept, and mourned <char style="add">[certain]</char> days, and fasted, and prayed before the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of heaven,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And said, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of heaven, the great and terrible God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that keeps covenant and mercy for them that love him and observe his commandments:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Let you<char style="ord">i</char> ear now be attentive, and you<char style="ord">i</char> eyes open, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may hear the prayer of you<char style="ord">i</char> servant, which I pray before you<char style="ord">i</char> now, day and night, for the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and confess the sins of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which we have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>: both I and my father’s house have sinned.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />We have dealt very corruptly against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and have not kept the commandments, nor the statutes, nor the judgments, which you<char style="ord">i</char> commanded you<char style="ord">i</char> servant Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Remember, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, the word that you<char style="ord">i</char> commanded you<char style="ord">i</char> servant Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, saying, <char style="add">[If]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> transgress, I will scatter you abroad among the nations:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But <char style="add">[if]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> turn unto me, and keep my commandments, and do them; though there were of you cast out unto the uttermost part of the heaven, <char style="add">[yet]</char> will I gather them from there, and will bring them unto the place that I have chosen to set my name there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> servants and you<char style="ord">i</char> people, whom you<char style="ord">i</char> have redeemed by you<char style="ord">i</char> great power, and by you<char style="ord">i</char> strong hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />O Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, let now you<char style="ord">i</char> ear be attentive to the prayer of you<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and to the prayer of you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, who desire to fear you<char style="ord">i</char> name: and prosper, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> servant this day, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man. For I was the king’s cupbearer.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the month Nisan <char style="add">[their flight]</char>, in the twentieth year of Artach’shashta <char style="add">[I will make the spoiled to boil: I will stir myself (in) winter]</char> the king, <char style="add">[that]</char> wine <char style="add">[was]</char> before him: and I took up the wine, and gave <char style="add">[it]</char> unto the king. Now I had not been <char style="add">[formerly]</char> sad in his presence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For what reason the king said unto me, Why <char style="add">[is]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char> sad, seeing you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> not sick? this <char style="add">[is]</char> nothing <char style="add">[else]</char> but sorrow of heart. Then I was very sore afraid,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And said unto the king, Let the king live forever: why should not my Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char> be sad, when the city, the place of my fathers’ sepulchres, <char style="add">[lies]</char> waste, and the gates thereof are consumed with fire?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then the king said unto me, For what do you<char style="ord">i</char> make request? So I prayed to the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I said unto the king, If it please the king, and if you<char style="ord">i</char> servant have found favour in you<char style="ord">i</char> sight, that you<char style="ord">i</char> would send me unto Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, unto the city of my fathers’ sepulchres, that I may build it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the king said unto me, <char style="pn">(the queen also sitting by him,)</char> For how long shall you<char style="ord">i</char> journey be? and when will you<char style="ord">i</char> return? So it pleased the king to send me; and I set him a time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Moreover I said unto the king, If it please the king, let letters be given me to the governors beyond the river, that they may convey me over till I come into Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And a letter unto Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char> the keeper of the king’s forest, that he may give me timber to make beams for the gates of the palace which <char style="add">[appertained]</char> to the house, and for the wall of the city, and for the house that I shall enter into. And the king granted me, according to the good hand of my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> upon me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then I came to the governors beyond the river, and gave them the king’s letters. Now the king had sent captains of the army and horsemen with me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />When Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> the Horoni <char style="add">[native of twin caves]</char>, and Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> the servant, the ‘Amoni <char style="add">[tribal]</char>, heard <char style="add">[of it]</char>, it grieved them exceedingly that there was come a man to seek the welfare of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />So I came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and was there three days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And I arose in the night, I and some few men with me; neither told I <char style="add">[any]</char> man what my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had put in my heart to do at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: neither <char style="add">[was there any]</char> beast with me, save the beast that I rode upon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I went out by night by the gate of the valley, even before the dragon well, and to the dung port, and viewed the walls of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, which were broken down, and the gates thereof were consumed with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then I went on to the gate of the fountain, and to the king’s pool: but <char style="add">[there was]</char> no place for the beast <char style="add">[that was]</char> under me to pass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then went I up in the night by the brook, and viewed the wall, and turned back, and entered by the gate of the valley, and <char style="add">[so]</char> returned.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the rulers knew not to which I went, or what I did; neither had I as yet told <char style="add">[it]</char> to the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char>, nor to the priests, nor to the nobles, nor to the rulers, nor to the rest that did the work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then said I unto them, You<char style="ord">2f</char> see the distress that we <char style="add">[are]</char> in, how Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace] [lies]</char> waste, and the gates thereof are burned with fire: come, and let us build up the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, that we be no more a reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then I told them of the hand of my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> which was good upon me; as also the king’s words that he had spoken unto me. And they said, Let us rise up and build. So they strengthened their hands for <char style="add">[this]</char> good <char style="add">[work]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />But when Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> the Horoni <char style="add">[native of twin caves]</char>, and Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> the servant, the ‘Amoni <char style="add">[tribal]</char>, and Geshem <char style="add">[rain]</char> the Aravi <char style="add">[Arabian]</char>, heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, they laughed us to scorn, and despised us, and said, What <char style="add">[is]</char> this thing that you<char style="ord">2f</char> do? will you<char style="ord">2f</char> rebel against the king?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then answered I them, and said unto them, The God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of heaven, he will prosper us; therefore we his servants will arise and build: but you<char style="ord">2f</char> have no portion, nor right, nor memorial, in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char> the High Priest rose up with his brethren the priests, and they built the Sheep Gate; they sanctified it, and set up the doors of it; even unto the tower of Me’ah <char style="add">[hundred]</char> they sanctified it, unto the tower of Hanan’el <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And next unto him built the men of Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>. And next to them built Zakur <char style="add">[Mindful]</char> the son of Imri <char style="add">[eloquent]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />But the fish gate did the sons of Hasna’ah <char style="add">[thorny]</char> build, who <char style="add">[also]</char> laid the beams thereof, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And next unto them repaired M’remot <char style="add">[elevations]</char> the son of Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char>, the son of Hakotz <char style="add">[thorn]</char>. And next unto them repaired Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char> the son of Berekhyah <char style="add">[Yehovah blesses]</char>, the son of Mesheizav’el <char style="add">[God delivers]</char>. And next unto them repaired Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the son of Ba’ana <char style="add">[in the affliction]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And next unto them the T’koi <char style="add">[trumpet blast]</char> repaired; but their nobles put not their necks to the work of their Lord-Adon <char style="add">[Lord of the Earth]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Moreover the old gate repaired Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the son of Paseach <char style="add">[limper]</char>, and Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char> the son of B’sodyah <char style="add">[with the counsel of Yehovah]</char>; they laid the beams thereof, and set up the doors thereof, and the locks thereof, and the bars thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And next unto them repaired M’latyah <char style="add">[Yehovah delivered]</char> the Giv’oni <char style="add">[little hill: hilly]</char>, and Yadon <char style="add">[thankful]</char> the Meronoti <char style="add">[joyful shouter]</char>, the men of Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>, and of Mitzpah <char style="add">[watchtower]</char>, unto the throne of the governor on this side the river.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Next unto him repaired Uzziel <char style="add">[My Strength is God]</char> the son of Harhayah <char style="add">[fear of Yehovah]</char>, of the goldsmiths. Next unto him also repaired Hananyah <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char> the son of <char style="add">[one of]</char> the apothecaries, and they fortified Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> unto the broad wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And next unto them repaired Refayah <char style="add">[healed of Yehovah]</char> the son of Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char>, the ruler of the half part of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And next unto them repaired Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char> the son of Harumaf <char style="add">[split nose]</char>, even over against his house. And next unto him repaired Hatush <char style="add">[assembled]</char> the son of Hashavn’yah <char style="add">[whom Yehovah regards]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Malkiyah <char style="add">[my king is Yehovah]</char> the son of Harim <char style="add">[dedicated]</char>, and Hashuv <char style="add">[considerate]</char> the son of Pachat-Mo’av <char style="add">[pit of Mo’av]</char>, repaired the other piece, and the tower of the furnaces.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And next unto him repaired Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char> the son of HaLochesh <char style="add">[whisperer]</char>, the ruler of the half part of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, he and his daughters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />The valley gate repaired Hanun <char style="add">[gracious]</char>, and the inhabitants of Zanoach <char style="add">[Cast Off]</char>; they built it, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof, and a thousand cubits on the wall unto the dung gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But the dung gate repaired Malkiyah <char style="add">[my king is Yehovah]</char> the son of Rekhav <char style="add">[rider]</char>, the ruler of part of Beit-Hakerem <char style="add">[house of the vineyard]</char>; he built it, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But the gate of the fountain repaired Shalun <char style="add">[retribution]</char> the son of Kol-Hozah <char style="add">[all-seeing]</char>, the ruler of part of Mitzpah <char style="add">[watchtower]</char>; he built it, and covered it, and set up the doors thereof, the locks thereof, and the bars thereof, and the wall of the Pool of Shelach <char style="add">[sent]</char> by the king’s garden, and unto the stairs that go down from the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />After him repaired Nechemyah <char style="add">[God comforts]</char> the son of Azbuk <char style="add">[strong devistation]</char>, the ruler of the half part of Beit’Tzur <char style="add">[House of the Rock]</char>, unto <char style="add">[the place]</char> over against the sepulchres of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and to the pool that was made, and unto the house of the mighty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />After him repaired the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, Rechum <char style="add">[compassion]</char> the son of Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>. Next unto him repaired Hashavyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char>, the ruler of the half part of Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, in his part.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />After him repaired their brethren, Bavai <char style="add">[my goings]</char> the son of Henadad <char style="add">[favour of Hadad]</char>, the ruler of the half part of Ke’ilah <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And next to him repaired ‘Ezer <char style="add">[treasure]</char> the son of Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, the ruler of Mitzpah <char style="add">[watchtower]</char>, another piece over against the going up to the armoury at the turning <char style="add">[of the wall]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />After him Barukh <char style="add">[Blessed (Favored by God; happy; prosperous)]</char> the son of Zabai <char style="add">[pure]</char> earnestly repaired the other piece, from the turning <char style="add">[of the wall]</char> unto the door of the house of Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char> the High Priest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />After him repaired M’remot <char style="add">[elevations]</char> the son of Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char> the son of Hakotz <char style="add">[thorn]</char> another piece, from the door of the house of Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char> even to the end of the house of Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And after him repaired the priests, the men of the plain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />After him repaired Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> and Hashuv <char style="add">[considerate]</char> over against their house. After him repaired ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char> the son of ‘Ananyah <char style="add">[Yehovah clouds]</char> by his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />After him repaired Binui <char style="add">[built up]</char> the son of Henadad <char style="add">[favour of Hadad]</char> another piece, from the house of ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> unto the turning <char style="add">[of the wall]</char>, even unto the corner.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Palal <char style="add">[judge]</char> the son of Uzai <char style="add">[I shall have my sprinklings]</char>, over against the turning <char style="add">[of the wall]</char>, and the tower which lies out from the king’s high house, that <char style="add">[was]</char> by the court of the prison. After him P’dayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has ransomed]</char> the son of Par’osh <char style="add">[flea]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Moreover the temple servants dwelt in ‘Ofel <char style="add">[hill]</char>, unto <char style="add">[the place]</char> over against the water gate toward the east, and the tower that lies out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />After them the T’koi <char style="add">[trumpet blast]</char> repaired another piece, over against the great tower that lies out, even unto the wall of ‘Ofel <char style="add">[hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />From above the horse gate repaired the priests, every one over against his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />After them repaired Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the son of Immer <char style="add">[he has said]</char> over against his house. After him repaired also Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the son of Sh’khanyah <char style="add">[dweller with Yehovah]</char>, the keeper of the east gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />After him repaired Hananyah <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char> the son of Shelemyah <char style="add">[repaid by Yehovah] [repaid by Yehovah]</char>, and Hanun <char style="add">[gracious]</char> the sixth son of Tzalaf <char style="add">[wound]</char>, another piece. After him repaired Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char> the son of Berekhyah <char style="add">[Yehovah blesses]</char> over against his chamber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />After him repaired Malkiyah <char style="add">[my king is Yehovah]</char> the goldsmith’s son unto the place of the temple servants, and of the merchants, over against the Gate Mif’kad <char style="add">[command]</char>, and to the going up of the corner.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And between the going up of the corner unto the Sheep Gate repaired the goldsmiths and the merchants.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />But it came to pass, that when Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> heard that we built the wall, he was exceedingly angry, and took great indignation, and mocked the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he spoke before his brethren and the army of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and said, What do these feeble Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char>? will they fortify themselves? will they sacrifice? will they make an end in a day? will they revive the stones out of the heaps of the rubbish which are burned?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> the ‘Amoni <char style="add">[tribal] [was]</char> by him, and he said, Even that which they build, if a fox go up, he shall even break down their stone wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Hear, O our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; for we are despised: and turn their reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> upon their own head, and give them for a prey in the land of captivity:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And cover not their iniquity, and let not their sin be blotted out from before you<char style="ord">i</char>: for they have provoked <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> to anger before the builders.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So built we the wall; and all the wall was joined together unto the half thereof: for the people had a mind to work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> when Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char>, and Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, and the Arabians, and the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and the Ashdodites, heard that the walls of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> were made up, <char style="add">[and]</char> that the breaches began to be stopped, then they were very exceedingly angry,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And conspired all of them together to come <char style="add">[and]</char> to fight against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and to hinder it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Nevertheless we made our prayer unto our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and set a watch against them day and night, because of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> said, The strength of the bearers of burdens is decayed, and <char style="add">[there is]</char> much rubbish; so that we are not able to build the wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And our adversaries said, They shall not know, neither see, till we come in the midst among them, and slay them, and cause the work to cease.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And it came to pass, that when the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char> which dwelt by them came, they said unto us ten times, From all places from what place you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall return unto us <char style="add">[they will be upon you]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Therefore set I in the lower places behind the wall, <char style="add">[and]</char> on the higher places, I even set the people after their families with their swords, their spears, and their bows.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I looked, and rose up, and said unto the nobles, and to the rulers, and to the rest of the people, Be not you<char style="ord">2f</char> afraid of them: remember the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, <char style="add">[which is]</char> great and terrible, and fight for your brethren, your sons, and your daughters, your wives, and your houses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And it came to pass, when our enemies heard that it was known unto us, and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had brought their counsel to nothing, that we returned all of us to the wall, every one unto his work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass from that time forth, <char style="add">[that]</char> the half of my servants wrought in the work, and the other half of them held both the spears, the shields, and the bows, and the habergeons; and the rulers <char style="add">[were]</char> behind all the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />They which built on the wall, and they that bore burdens, with those that laded, <char style="add">[every one]</char> with one of his hands wrought in the work, and with the other <char style="add">[hand]</char> held a weapon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />For the builders, everyone had his sword girded by his side, and <char style="add">[so]</char> built. And he that sounded the trumpet <char style="add">[was]</char> by me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And I said unto the nobles, and to the rulers, and to the rest of the people, The work <char style="add">[is]</char> great and large, and we are separated upon the wall, one far from another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />In what place <char style="add">[therefore]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> hear the sound of the trumpet, resort you<char style="ord">2f</char> there unto us: our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shall fight for us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So we laboured in the work: and half of them held the spears from the rising of the morning till the stars appeared.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Likewise at the same time said I unto the people, Let everyone with his servant lodge within Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, that in the night they may be a guard to us, and labour on the day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So neither I, nor my brethren, nor my servants, nor the men of the guard which followed me, none of us put off our clothes, <char style="add">[saving that]</char> every one put them off for washing.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And there was a great cry of the people and of their wives against their brethren the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For there were that said, We, our sons, and our daughters, <char style="add">[are]</char> many: therefore we take up corn <char style="add">[for them]</char>, that we may eat, and live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Some]</char> also there were that said, We have mortgaged our lands, vineyards, and houses, that we might buy corn, because of the famine.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />There were also that said, We have borrowed money for the king’s tribute, <char style="add">[and that upon]</char> our lands and vineyards.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Yet now our flesh <char style="add">[is]</char> as the flesh of our brethren, our children as their children: and, lo, we bring into bondage our sons and our daughters to be servants, and <char style="add">[some]</char> of our daughters are brought unto bondage <char style="add">[already]</char>: neither <char style="add">[is it]</char> in our power <char style="add">[to redeem them]</char>; for other men have our lands and vineyards.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I was very angry when I heard their cry and these words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then I consulted with myself, and I rebuked the nobles, and the rulers, and said unto them, You<char style="ord">2f</char> exact usury <char style="pn">(interest paid for using money)</char>, every one of his brother. And I set a great assembly against them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I said unto them, We after our ability have redeemed our brethren the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char>, which were sold unto the heathen; and will you<char style="ord">2f</char> even sell your brethren? or shall they be sold unto us? Then held they their peace, and found nothing <char style="add">[to answer]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Also I said, It <char style="add">[is]</char> not good that you<char style="ord">2f</char> do: ought you<char style="ord">2f</char> not to walk in the fear of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> because of the reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> of the heathen our enemies?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />I likewise, <char style="add">[and]</char> my brethren, and my servants, might exact of them money and corn: I pray you, let us leave off this usury <char style="pn">(interest paid for using money)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Restore, I pray you, to them, even this day, their lands, their vineyards, their oliveyards, and their houses, also the hundredth <char style="add">[part]</char> of the money, and of the corn, the wine, and the oil, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> exact of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then said they, We will restore <char style="add">[them]</char>, and will require nothing of them; so will we do as you<char style="ord">i</char> say. Then I called the priests, and took an oath of them, that they should do according to this promise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Also I shook my lap, and said, So God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shake out every man from his house, and from his labour, that performs not this promise, even thus be he shaken out, and emptied. And all the congregation said, Amen, and praised the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And the people did according to this promise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Moreover from the time that I was appointed to be their governor in the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, from the twentieth year even unto the two and thirtieth year of Artach’shashta <char style="add">[I will make the spoiled to boil: I will stir myself (in) winter]</char> the king, <char style="add">[that is]</char>, twelve years, I and my brethren have not eaten the bread of the governor.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But the former governors that <char style="add">[had been]</char> before me were chargeable unto the people, and had taken of them bread and wine, beside forty shekels of silver; yes, even their servants bore rule over the people: but so did not I, because of the fear of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Yes, also I continued in the work of this wall, neither bought we any land: and all my servants <char style="add">[were]</char> gathered there unto the work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Moreover <char style="add">[there were]</char> at my table an hundred and fifty of the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char> and rulers, beside those that came unto us from among the heathen that <char style="add">[are]</char> about us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Now <char style="add">[that]</char> which was prepared <char style="add">[for me]</char> daily <char style="add">[was]</char> one ox <char style="add">[and]</char> six choice sheep; also fowls were prepared for me, and once in ten days store of all sorts of wine: yet for all this required not I the bread of the governor, because the bondage was heavy upon this people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Think upon me, my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, for good, <char style="add">[according]</char> to all that I have done for this people.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now it came to pass, when Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char>, and Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, and Geshem <char style="add">[rain]</char> the Aravi <char style="add">[Arabian]</char>, and the rest of our enemies, heard that I had built the wall, and <char style="add">[that]</char> there was no breach <char style="pn">(breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)</char> left in it; (though at that time I had not set up the doors upon the gates;)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />That Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> and Geshem <char style="add">[rain]</char> sent unto me, saying, Come, let us meet together in <char style="add">[some one of]</char> the villages in the plain of Ono <char style="add">[vigorous]</char>. But they thought to do me mischief.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I sent messengers unto them, saying, I <char style="add">[am]</char> doing a great work, so that I cannot come down: why should the work cease, whilst I leave it, and come down to you?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Yet they sent unto me four times after this sort; and I answered them after the same manner.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then sent Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> his servant unto me in like manner the fifth time with an open letter in his hand;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Wherein <char style="add">[was]</char> written, It is reported among the heathen, and Geshemu <char style="add">[rain]</char> says <char style="add">[it, that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> and the Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char> think to rebel: for which cause you<char style="ord">i</char> build the wall, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may be their king, according to these words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> have also appointed prophets to preach of you<char style="ord">i</char> at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, saying, <char style="add">[There is]</char> a king in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: and now shall it be reported to the king according to these words. Come now therefore, and let us take counsel together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then I sent unto him, saying, There are no such things done as you<char style="ord">i</char> say, but you<char style="ord">i</char> pretend them out of you<char style="ord">i</char> own heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For they all made us afraid, saying, Their hands shall be weakened from the work, that it be not done. Now therefore, <char style="add">[O God-Elōhīm (The Living Word) [The Many Powered]]</char>, strengthen my hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Afterward I came unto the house of Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the son of D’layahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has accomplished]</char> the son of M’heitav’el <char style="add">[Favoured of God]</char>, who <char style="add">[was]</char> shut up; and he said, Let us meet together in the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, within the temple, and let us shut the doors of the temple: for they will come to slay you<char style="ord">i</char>; yes, in the night will they come to slay you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And I said, Should such a man as I flee? and who <char style="add">[is there]</char>, that, <char style="add">[being]</char> as I <char style="add">[am]</char>, would go into the temple to save his life? I will not go in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And, lo, I perceived that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had not sent him; but that he pronounced this prophecy against me: for Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> and Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> had hired him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Therefore <char style="add">[was]</char> he hired, that I should be afraid, and do so, and sin, and <char style="add">[that]</char> they might have <char style="add">[matter]</char> for an evil report, that they might reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />My God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, think you<char style="ord">i</char> upon Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> and Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> according to these their works, and on the prophetess No’adyah <char style="add">[meeting with Yehovah]</char>, and the rest of the prophets, that would have put me in fear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So the wall was finished in the twenty and fifth <char style="add">[day]</char> of <char style="add">[the month]</char> Elul, in fifty and two days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass, that when all our enemies heard <char style="add">[thereof]</char>, and all the heathen that <char style="add">[were]</char> about us saw <char style="add">[these things]</char>, they were much cast down in their own eyes: for they perceived that this work was wrought of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Moreover in those days the nobles of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> sent many letters unto Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, and <char style="add">[the letters]</char> of Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> came unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />For <char style="add">[there were]</char> many in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> sworn unto him, because he <char style="add">[was]</char> the son in law of Sh’khanyah <char style="add">[dweller with Yehovah]</char> the son of Arach <char style="add">[traveller]</char>; and his son Yochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char> had taken the daughter of Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char> the son of Berekhyah <char style="add">[Yehovah blesses]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Also they reported his good deeds before me, and uttered my words to him. <char style="add">[And]</char> Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> sent letters to put me in fear.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now it came to pass, when the wall was built, and I had set up the doors, and the porters and the singers and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> were appointed,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />That I gave my brother Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char>, and Hananyah <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char> the ruler of the palace, charge over Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: for he <char style="add">[was]</char> a faithful man, and feared God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> above many.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I said unto them, Let not the gates of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> be opened until the sun be hot; and while they stand by, let them shut the doors, and bar <char style="add">[them]</char>: and appoint watches of the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, everyone in his watch, and every one <char style="add">[to be]</char> over against his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Now the city <char style="add">[was]</char> large and great: but the people <char style="add">[were]</char> few in it, and the houses <char style="add">[were]</char> not built.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> put into my heart to gather together the nobles, and the rulers, and the people, that they might be reckoned by genealogy. And I found a register of the genealogy of them which came up at the first, and found written in it,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />These <char style="add">[are]</char> the children of the province, that went up out of the captivity, of those that had been carried away, whom N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> had carried away, and came again to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, every one unto his city;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Who came with Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char>, Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, Nechemyah <char style="add">[God comforts]</char>, ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, Ra’amyah <char style="add">[thunder of Yehovah]</char>, Nachamani <char style="add">[merciful]</char>, Mordekhai <char style="add">[little man]</char>, Bilshan <char style="add">[in slander]</char>, Misperet <char style="add">[number]</char>, Bigvai <char style="add">[in my bodies]</char>, N’chum <char style="add">[comfort]</char>, Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char>. The number, <char style="add">[I say]</char>, of the men of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [was this]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The children of Par’osh <char style="add">[flea]</char>, two thousand an hundred seventy and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The children of Sh’fatyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, three hundred seventy and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />The children of Arach <char style="add">[traveller]</char>, six hundred fifty and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />The children of Pachat-Mo’av <char style="add">[pit of Mo’av]</char>, of the children of Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char> and Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, two thousand and eight hundred <char style="add">[and]</char> eighteen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The children of ‘Eilam <char style="add">[eternity]</char>, a thousand two hundred fifty and four.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />The children of Zatu <char style="add">[brightness of him]</char>, eight hundred forty and five.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The children of Zakkai <char style="add">[pure]</char>, seven hundred and threescore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The children of Binui <char style="add">[built up]</char>, six hundred forty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />The children of Bevai <char style="add">[my cavities]</char>, six hundred twenty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />The children of ‘Azgad <char style="add">[Gad is mighty]</char>, two thousand three hundred twenty and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The children of Adonikam <char style="add">[my lord arose]</char>, six hundred threescore and seven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />The children of Bigvai <char style="add">[in my bodies]</char>, two thousand threescore and seven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />The children of ‘Adin <char style="add">[delicate]</char>, six hundred fifty and five.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />The children of Ater <char style="add">[binder]</char> of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, ninety and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />The children of Hashum <char style="add">[rich]</char>, three hundred twenty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />The children of Betzai <char style="add">[conqueror]</char>, three hundred twenty and four.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />The children of Harif <char style="add">[a plucking off]</char>, an hundred and twelve.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />The children of Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>, ninety and five.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />The men of Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char> and N’tofah <char style="add">[dropping]</char>, an hundred eighty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />The men of ‘Anatot <char style="add">[answers to prayer]</char>, an hundred twenty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />The men of Beit-’Azmavet <char style="add">[house of the strength of death]</char>, forty and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />The men of Kiryat-Ye’arim <char style="add">[City of Forests]</char>, K’firah <char style="add">[Lioness]</char>, and B’erot <char style="add">[Wells]</char>, seven hundred forty and three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />The men of Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char> and Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char>, six hundred twenty and one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />The men of Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char>, an hundred and twenty and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />The men of Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> and ‘Ai <char style="add">[Heap of Ruins]</char>, an hundred twenty and three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />The men of the other Nevo <char style="add">[Prophet]</char>, fifty and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />The children of the other ‘Eilam <char style="add">[eternity]</char>, a thousand two hundred fifty and four.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />The children of Harim <char style="add">[dedicated]</char>, three hundred and twenty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />The children of Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>, three hundred forty and five.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />The children of Lod <char style="add">[travail]</char>, Hadid <char style="add">[sharp]</char>, and Ono <char style="add">[vigorous]</char>, seven hundred twenty and one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />The children of S’na’ah <char style="add">[thorny]</char>, three thousand nine hundred and thirty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />The priests: the children of Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char>, of the house of Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, nine hundred seventy and three.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />The children of Immer <char style="add">[he has said]</char>, a thousand fifty and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />The children of Pash’chur <char style="add">[freedom]</char>, a thousand two hundred forty and seven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />The children of Harim <char style="add">[dedicated]</char>, a thousand and seventeen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />The Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: the children of Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, of Kadmi’el <char style="add">[God is the ancient one]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> of the children of Hodvah <char style="add">[praise of Yehovah]</char>, seventy and four.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />The singers: the children of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>, an hundred forty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />The porters: the children of Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char>, the children of Ater <char style="add">[binder]</char>, the children of Talmon <char style="add">[oppressor]</char>, the children of ‘Akuv <char style="add">[insidious]</char>, the children of Hatita <char style="add">[exploring]</char>, the children of Shovai <char style="add">[glorious]</char>, an hundred thirty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />The temple servants: the children of Tzicha <char style="add">[parched]</char>, the children of Hasufa <char style="add">[stipped]</char>, the children of Taba’ot <char style="add">[rings]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />The children of Keros <char style="add">[anklet]</char>, the children of Si’a <char style="add">[departing]</char>, the children of Padon <char style="add">[ransom]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />The children of L’vanah <char style="add">[moon-white]</char>, the children of Hagava <char style="add">[locust]</char>, the children of Salmai <char style="add">[my garments]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />The children of Hanan <char style="add">[he is merciful]</char>, the children of Giddel <char style="add">[very great]</char>, the children of Gachar <char style="add">[hiding place]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />The children of Re’ayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has seen]</char>, the children of Retzin <char style="add">[firm]</char>, the children of N’koda <char style="add">[distinguished]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />The children of Gazam <char style="add">[devouring]</char>, the children of ‘Uza <char style="add">[strength]</char>, the children of Paseach <char style="add">[limper]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />The children of Besai <char style="add">[my treading]</char>, the children of Me’unim <char style="add">[habitations]</char>, the children of N’fish’sim <char style="add">[refreshed of spices]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" />The children of Bakbuk <char style="add">[bottle]</char>, the children of Hakufa <char style="add">[bent]</char>, the children of Harhur <char style="add">[inflammation]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" />The children of Batzlit <char style="add">[asking]</char>, the children of M’chida <char style="add">[famour, or noble]</char>, the children of Harsha <char style="add">[mute]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="55" style="v" />The children of Barkos <char style="add">[the son cut off]</char>, the children of Sisra [Battle Array (to put on; to clothe)], the children of Temach <char style="add">[laughter]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" />The children of N’tziach <char style="add">[pre-eminent]</char>, the children of Hatifa <char style="add">[seized]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" />The children of Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> servants: the children of Sotai <char style="add">[changeful]</char>, the children of HaSoferet <char style="add">[writing]</char>, the children of P’rida <char style="add">[grain]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" />The children of Ya’lah <char style="add">[ascending]</char>, the children of Darkon <char style="add">[scatterer]</char>, the children of Giddel <char style="add">[very great]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" />The children of Sh’fatyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, the children of Hatil <char style="add">[doubtful]</char>, the children of Pokheret-Hatzvayim <char style="add">[here is the cutting off]</char>, the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="60" style="v" />All the temple servants, and the children of Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> servants, <char style="add">[were]</char> three hundred ninety and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="61" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[were]</char> they which went up <char style="add">[also]</char> from Tel-Melach <char style="add">[mound of salt]</char>, Tel-Harsha <char style="add">[mound of the deaf mute]</char>, K’ruv <char style="add">[blessing]</char>, Adon <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and Immer <char style="add">[he has said]</char>: but they could not show their father’s house, nor their seed, whether they <char style="add">[were]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="62" style="v" />The children of D’layahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has accomplished]</char>, the children of Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, the children of N’koda <char style="add">[distinguished]</char>, six hundred forty and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="63" style="v" />And of the priests: the children of Havayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has hidden]</char>, the children of Hakotz <char style="add">[thorn]</char>, the children of Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char>, which took <char style="add">[one]</char> of the daughters of Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char> the Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char> to wife, and was called after their name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="64" style="v" />These sought their register <char style="add">[among]</char> those that were reckoned by genealogy, but it was not found: therefore were they, as polluted, put from the priesthood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="65" style="v" />And the Tirshata <char style="add">[governor]</char> said unto them, that they should not eat of the most holy things, till there stood <char style="add">[up]</char> a priest with Urim <char style="add">[Lights]</char> and Tumim <char style="add">[Perfection]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="66" style="v" />The whole congregation together <char style="add">[was]</char> forty and two thousand three hundred and threescore,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="67" style="v" />Beside their manservants and their maidservants, of whom <char style="add">[there were]</char> seven thousand three hundred thirty and seven: and they had two hundred forty and five singing men and singing women.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="68" style="v" />Their horses, seven hundred thirty and six: their mules, two hundred forty and five:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="69" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Their]</char> camels, four hundred thirty and five: six thousand seven hundred and twenty asses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="70" style="v" />And some of the chief of the fathers gave unto the work. The Tirshata <char style="add">[governor]</char> gave to the treasure a thousand drams of gold, fifty basons, five hundred and thirty priests’ garments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="71" style="v" />And <char style="add">[some]</char> of the chief of the fathers gave to the treasure of the work twenty thousand drams of gold, and two thousand and two hundred pound of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="72" style="v" />And <char style="add">[that]</char> which the rest of the people gave <char style="add">[was]</char> twenty thousand drams of gold, and two thousand pound of silver, and threescore and seven priests’ garments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="73" style="v" />So the priests, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and the porters, and the singers, and <char style="add">[some]</char> of the people, and the temple servants, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, dwelt in their cities; and when the seventh month came, the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [were]</char> in their cities.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And all the people gathered themselves together as one man into the street that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the water gate; and they spoke unto ‘the scribe to bring the book of the law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And ‘the priest brought the law before the congregation both of men and women, and all that could hear with understanding, upon the first day of the seventh month.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he read in it before the street that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the water gate from the morning until midday, before the men and the women, and those that could understand; and the ears of all the people <char style="add">[were attentive]</char> unto the book of the law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And ‘the scribe stood upon a pulpit of wood, which they had made for the purpose; and beside him stood Mattityah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>, and Sh’ma <char style="add">[Hear]</char>, and ‘Anayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has answered]</char>, and Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my flame]</char>, and Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, and Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char>, on his right hand; and on his left hand, P’dayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has ransomed]</char>, and Misha’el <char style="add">[Who is what God is]</char>, and Malkiyah <char style="add">[my king is Yehovah]</char>, and Hashum <char style="add">[rich]</char>, and Hashbadanah <char style="add">[considerate judge]</char>, Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And ‘opened the book in the sight of all the people; <char style="pn">(for he was above all the people;)</char> and when he opened it, all the people stood up:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And ‘Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the great God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. And all the people answered, Amen, Amen, with lifting up their hands: and they bowed their heads, and worshipped the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with <char style="add">[their]</char> faces to the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Also Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, and Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>, and Sherevyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has scorched]</char>, Yamin <char style="add">[Right Hand]</char>, ‘Akuv <char style="add">[insidious]</char>, Shabtai <char style="add">[sabbatical]</char>, Hodiyah <char style="add">[my majesty is Yehovah]</char>, Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char>, K’lita <char style="add">[crippled]</char>, ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, Yozavad <char style="add">[Yehovah has endowed]</char>, Hanan <char style="add">[he is merciful]</char>, P’layah <char style="add">[Yehovah does wonders]</char>, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, caused the people to understand the law: and the people <char style="add">[stood]</char> in their place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So they read in the book in the law of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> distinctly, and gave the sense, and caused <char style="add">[them]</char> to understand the reading.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Nechemyah <char style="add">[God comforts]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> the Tirshata <char style="add">[governor]</char>, and ‘the priest the scribe, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that taught the people, said unto all the people, This day <char style="add">[is]</char> holy unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; mourn not, nor weep. For all the people wept, when they heard the words of the law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then he said unto them, Go your way, eat the fat, and drink the sweet, and send portions unto them for whom nothing is prepared: for <char style="add">[this]</char> day <char style="add">[is]</char> holy unto our Lord: neither be you<char style="ord">2f</char> sorry; for the joy of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> is your strength.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />So the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> stilled all the people, saying, Hold your peace, for the day <char style="add">[is]</char> holy; neither be you<char style="ord">2f</char> grieved.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And all the people went their way to eat, and to drink, and to send portions, and to make great gladness, because they had understood the words that were declared unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And on the second day were gathered together the chief of the fathers of all the people, the priests, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, unto ‘the scribe, even to understand the words of the law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they found written in the law which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had commanded by Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, that the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> should dwell in booths in the feast of the seventh month:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And that they should publish and proclaim in all their cities, and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, saying, Go forth unto the mount, and fetch olive branches, and pine branches, and myrtle branches, and palm branches, and branches of thick trees, to make booths, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />So the people went forth, and brought <char style="add">[them]</char>, and made themselves booths, every one upon the roof of his house, and in their courts, and in the courts of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and in the street of the water gate, and in the street of the gate of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And all the congregation of them that were come again out of the captivity made booths, and sat under the booths: for since the days of Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char> the son of Nun <char style="add">[Posterity]</char> unto that day had not the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> done so. And there was very great gladness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Also day by day, from the first day unto the last day, he read in the book of the law of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. And they kept the feast seven days; and on the eighth day <char style="add">[was]</char> a solemn assembly, according unto the manner.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now in the twenty and fourth day of this month the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were assembled with fasting, and with sackclothes, and earth upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the seed of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> separated themselves from all strangers, and stood and confessed their sins, and the iniquities of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they stood up in their place, and read in the book of the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [one]</char> fourth part of the day; and <char style="add">[another]</char> fourth part they confessed, and worshipped the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then stood up upon the stairs, of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, and Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>, Kadmi’el <char style="add">[God is the ancient one]</char>, Sh’vanyah <char style="add">[increased by Yehovah]</char>, Buni <char style="add">[built]</char>, Sherevyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has scorched]</char>, Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> K’nani <char style="add">[my station]</char>, and cried with a loud voice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, and Kadmi’el <char style="add">[God is the ancient one]</char>, Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>, Hashavn’yah <char style="add">[whom Yehovah regards]</char>, Sherevyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has scorched]</char>, Hodiyah <char style="add">[my majesty is Yehovah]</char>, Sh’vanyah <char style="add">[increased by Yehovah]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> P’tachyah <char style="add">[freed by Yehovah]</char>, said, Stand up <char style="add">[and]</char> bless the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> forever and ever: and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> be you<char style="ord">i</char> glorious name, which is exalted above all blessing and praise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[are]</char> LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> alone; you<char style="ord">i</char> have made heaven, the heaven of heavens, with all their host, the earth, and all <char style="add">[things]</char> that <char style="add">[are]</char> in it, the seas, and all that <char style="add">[is]</char> in it, and you<char style="ord">i</char> preserve them all; and the army of heaven worships you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, who did choose Abram, and brought him forth out of Ur of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers] [clod-breakers]</char>, and gave him the name of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And found his heart faithful before you<char style="ord">i</char>, and made a covenant with him to give the land of the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, and the Girgashi <char style="add">[Dwelling on Clay Soil]</char>, to give <char style="add">[it, I say]</char>, to his seed, and have performed you<char style="ord">i</char> words; for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> righteous:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And did see the affliction of our fathers in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and heard their cry by the Red sea;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And showed signs and wonders upon Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, and on all his servants, and on all the people of his land: for you<char style="ord">i</char> knew that they dealt proudly against them. So did you<char style="ord">i</char> get yourselfi a name, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> did divide the sea before them, so that they went through the midst of the sea on the dry land; and their persecutors you<char style="ord">i</char> threw into the deeps, as a stone into the mighty waters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Moreover you<char style="ord">i</char> led them in the day by a cloudy pillar; and in the night by a pillar of fire, to give them light in the way wherein they should go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> came down also upon mount Sinai, and spoke with them from heaven, and gave them right judgments, and true laws, good statutes and commandments:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And made known unto them you<char style="ord">i</char> holy Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, and commanded them precepts, statutes, and laws, by the hand of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> servant:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And gave them bread from heaven for their hunger, and brought forth water for them out of the rock for their thirst, and promised them that they should go in to possess the land which you<char style="ord">i</char> had sworn to give them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But they and our fathers dealt proudly, and hardened their necks, and listened not to you<char style="ord">i</char> commandments,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And refused to obey, neither were mindful of you<char style="ord">i</char> wonders that you<char style="ord">i</char> did among them; but hardened their necks, and in their rebellion appointed a captain to return to their bondage: but you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> ready to pardon, gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and forsook them not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Yes, when they had made them a molten calf, and said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> that brought you<char style="ord">i</char> up out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and had wrought great provocations;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Yet you<char style="ord">i</char> in your<char style="ord">i</char> manifold mercies forsook them not in the wilderness: the pillar of the cloud departed not from them by day, to lead them in the way; neither the pillar of fire by night, to show them light, and the way wherein they should go.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> gave also your<char style="ord">i</char> good spirit to instruct them, and withheld not your<char style="ord">i</char> manna from their mouth, and gave them water for their thirst.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Yes, forty years did you<char style="ord">i</char> sustain them in the wilderness, <char style="add">[so that]</char> they lacked nothing; their clothes waxed not old, and their feet swelled not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Moreover you<char style="ord">i</char> gave them kingdoms and nations, and did divide them into corners: so they possessed the land of Sichon <char style="add">[Warrior]</char>, and the land of the king of Heshbon <char style="add">[Stronghold]</char>, and the land of ‘Og <char style="add">[Long-necked]</char> king of Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Their children also multiplied you<char style="ord">i</char> as the stars of heaven, and brought them into the land, concerning which you<char style="ord">i</char> had promised to their fathers, that they should go in to possess <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />So the children went in and possessed the land, and you<char style="ord">i</char> subdued before them the inhabitants of the land, the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>, and gave them into their hands, with their kings, and the people of the land, that they might do with them as they would.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they took strong cities, and a fat land, and possessed houses full of all goods, wells excavated, vineyards, and oliveyards, and fruit trees in abundance: so they did eat, and were filled, and became fat, and delighted themselves in you<char style="ord">i</char> great goodness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Nevertheless they were disobedient, and rebelled against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and cast you<char style="ord">i</char> law behind their backs, and killed you<char style="ord">i</char> prophets which testified against them to turn them to you<char style="ord">i</char>, and they wrought great provocations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> delivered them into the hand of their enemies, who vexed them: and in the time of their trouble, when they cried unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> heard <char style="add">[them]</char> from heaven; and according to you<char style="ord">i</char> manifold mercies you<char style="ord">i</char> gave them saviours, who saved them out of the hand of their enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />But after they had rest, they did evil again before you<char style="ord">i</char>: therefore left you<char style="ord">i</char> them in the hand of their enemies, so that they had the dominion over them: yet when they returned, and cried unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> heard <char style="add">[them]</char> from heaven; and many times did you<char style="ord">i</char> deliver them according to you<char style="ord">i</char> mercies;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And testified against them, that you<char style="ord">i</char> might bring them again unto you<char style="ord">i</char> law: yet they dealt proudly, and listened not unto you<char style="ord">i</char> commandments, but sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char> judgments, <char style="pn">(which if a man do, he shall live in them;)</char> and withdrew the shoulder, and hardened their neck, and would not hear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Yet many years did you<char style="ord">i</char> refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char> them, and testified against them by you<char style="ord">i</char> spirit in you<char style="ord">i</char> prophets: yet would they not give ear: therefore gave you<char style="ord">i</char> them into the hand of the people of the lands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Nevertheless for you<char style="ord">i</char> great mercies’ sake you<char style="ord">i</char> did not utterly consume them, nor forsake them; for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a gracious and merciful God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Now therefore, our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, the great, the mighty, and the terrible God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, who keeps covenant and mercy, let not all the trouble seem little before you<char style="ord">i</char>, that has come upon us, on our kings, on our princes, and on our priests, and on our prophets, and on our fathers, and on all you<char style="ord">i</char> people, since the time of the kings of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />However you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> just in all that is brought upon us; for you<char style="ord">i</char> have done right, but we have done wickedly:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Neither have our kings, our princes, our priests, nor our fathers, kept you<char style="ord">i</char> law, nor listened unto you<char style="ord">i</char> commandments and you<char style="ord">i</char> testimonies, which you<char style="ord">i</char> did testify against them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />For they have not served you<char style="ord">i</char> in their kingdom, and in you<char style="ord">i</char> great goodness that you<char style="ord">i</char> gave them, and in the large and fat land which you<char style="ord">i</char> gave before them, neither turned they from their wicked works.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Behold, we <char style="add">[are]</char> servants this day, and <char style="add">[for]</char> the land that you<char style="ord">i</char> gave unto our fathers to eat the fruit thereof and the good thereof, behold, we <char style="add">[are]</char> servants in it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And it yielded much increase unto the kings whom you<char style="ord">i</char> have set over us because of our sins: also they have dominion over our bodies, and over our cattle, at their pleasure, and we <char style="add">[are]</char> in great distress.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And because of all this we make a sure <char style="add">[covenant]</char>, and write <char style="add">[it]</char>; and our princes, Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> priests, seal <char style="add">[unto it]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now those that sealed <char style="add">[were]</char>, Nechemyah <char style="add">[God comforts]</char>, the Tirshata <char style="add">[governor]</char>, the son of Hakhalyah <char style="add">[whom Yehovah enlightens]</char>, and Tzedekyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />S’rayah <char style="add">[Yehovah is ruler]</char>, ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Pash’chur <char style="add">[freedom]</char>, Amaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah speaks]</char>, Malkiyah <char style="add">[my king is Yehovah]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Hatush <char style="add">[assembled]</char>, Sh’vanyah <char style="add">[increased by Yehovah]</char>, Malukh <char style="add">[counselor]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Harim <char style="add">[dedicated]</char>, M’remot <char style="add">[elevations]</char>, ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Dani’el <char style="add">[God is Judge]</char>, Ginton <char style="add">[gardener]</char>, Barukh [Blessed (Favored by God; happy; prosperous)],</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>, Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>, Minyamin <char style="add">[from the right hand]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Ma’azyah <char style="add">[consolation of Yehovah]</char>, Bilgai <char style="add">[my cheerfulness]</char>, Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>: these <char style="add">[were]</char> the priests.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: both Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char> the son of Azanyah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, Binui <char style="add">[built up]</char> of the sons of Henadad <char style="add">[favour of Hadad]</char>, Kadmi’el <char style="add">[God is the ancient one]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And their brethren, Sh’vanyah <char style="add">[increased by Yehovah]</char>, Hodiyah <char style="add">[my majesty is Yehovah]</char>, K’lita <char style="add">[crippled]</char>, P’layah <char style="add">[Yehovah does wonders]</char>, Hanan <char style="add">[he is merciful]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Mikha <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, Rechov <char style="add">[Broad Place]</char>, Hashavyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Zakur <char style="add">[Mindful]</char>, Sherevyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has scorched]</char>, Sh’vanyah <char style="add">[increased by Yehovah]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Hodiyah <char style="add">[my majesty is Yehovah]</char>, Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>, B’ninu <char style="add">[our son]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The chief of the people; Par’osh <char style="add">[flea]</char>, Pachat-Mo’av <char style="add">[pit of Mo’av]</char>, ‘Eilam <char style="add">[eternity]</char>, Zatu <char style="add">[brightness of him]</char>, Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Buni <char style="add">[built]</char>, ‘Azgad <char style="add">[Gad is mighty]</char>, Bevai <char style="add">[my cavities]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>, Bigvai <char style="add">[in my bodies]</char>, ‘Adin <char style="add">[delicate]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Ater <char style="add">[binder]</char>, Hizkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, ‘Azur <char style="add">[he that assists]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Hodiyah <char style="add">[my majesty is Yehovah]</char>, Hashum <char style="add">[rich]</char>, Betzai <char style="add">[conqueror]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Harif <char style="add">[a plucking off]</char>, ‘Anatot <char style="add">[answers to prayer]</char>, Neivai <char style="add">[fruitful]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Magpi’ash <char style="add">[moth-killer]</char>, Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>, Hezir <char style="add">[swine]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Mesheizav’el <char style="add">[God delivers]</char>, Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>, Yadua <char style="add">[knowing]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />P’latyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah delivers]</char>, Hanan <char style="add">[he is merciful]</char>, ‘Anayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has answered]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Hoshea <char style="add">[salvation]</char>, Hananyah <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char>, Hashuv <char style="add">[considerate]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />HaLochesh <char style="add">[whisperer]</char>, Pilcha <char style="add">[slicing]</char>, Shovek <char style="add">[free]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Rechum <char style="add">[compassion]</char>, Hashavnah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char>, Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>, Hanan <char style="add">[he is merciful]</char>, Anan,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Malukh <char style="add">[counselor]</char>, Harim <char style="add">[dedicated]</char>, Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the rest of the people, the priests, the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, the porters, the singers, the temple servants, and all they that had separated themselves from the people of the lands unto the law of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, their wives, their sons, and their daughters, every one having knowledge, and having understanding;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />They clave to their brethren, their nobles, and entered into a curse, and into an oath, to walk in God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>’s law, which was given by Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> the servant of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and to observe and do all the commandments of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our Lord-Adon <char style="add">[Lord of the Earth]</char>, and his judgments and his statutes;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And that we would not give our daughters unto the people of the land, nor take their daughters for our sons:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And <char style="add">[if]</char> the people of the land bring ware or any victuals <char style="pn">(food for humans)</char> on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day to sell, <char style="add">[that]</char> we would not buy it of them on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, or on the holy day: and <char style="add">[that]</char> we would leave the seventh year, and the exaction of every debt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Also we made ordinances for us, to charge ourselves yearly with the third part of a shekel for the service of the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />For the showbread, and for the continual meat offering, and for the continual burnt offering, of the Shabbat, of the new moons, for the set feasts, and for the holy <char style="add">[things]</char>, and for the sin offerings to make an atonement for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and <char style="add">[for]</char> all the work of the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And we cast the lots among the priests, the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and the people, for the wood offering, to bring <char style="add">[it]</char> into the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, after the houses of our fathers, at times appointed year by year, to burn upon the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the law:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And to bring the firstfruits of our ground, and the firstfruits of all fruit of all trees, year by year, unto the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Also the firstborn of our sons, and of our cattle, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the law, and the firstlings of our herds and of our flocks, to bring to the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, unto the priests that minister in the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And <char style="add">[that]</char> we should bring the firstfruits of our dough, and our offerings, and the fruit of all manner of trees, of wine and of oil, unto the priests, to the chambers of the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and the tithes of our ground unto the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, that the same Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> might have the tithes in all the cities of our tillage.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the priest the son of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> shall be with the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, when the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> take tithes: and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> shall bring up the tithe of the tithes unto the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to the chambers, into the treasure house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />For the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and the children of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char> shall bring the offering of the corn, of the New Wine, and the oil, unto the chambers, where <char style="add">[are]</char> the vessels of the sanctuary, and the priests that minister, and the porters, and the singers: and we will not forsake the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the rulers of the people dwelt at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: the rest of the people also cast lots, to bring one of ten to dwell in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> the holy city, and nine parts <char style="add">[to dwell]</char> in <char style="add">[other]</char> cities.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the people Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> all the men, that willingly offered themselves to dwell at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> the chief of the province that dwelt in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: but in the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> dwelt everyone in his possession in their cities, <char style="add">[that is to say]</char>, Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, the priests, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and the temple servants, and the children of Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> dwelt <char style="add">[certain]</char> of the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and of the children of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>. Of the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; ‘Atayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char>, the son of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, the son of Amaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah speaks]</char>, the son of Sh’fatyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, the son of Mahalal’el <char style="add">[praise of God]</char>, of the children of Peretz <char style="add">[breach (breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char> the son of Barukh <char style="add">[Blessed (Favored by God; happy; prosperous)]</char>, the son of Kol-Hozah <char style="add">[all-seeing]</char>, the son of Hazayah <char style="add">[God has seen]</char>, the son of ‘Adayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has adorned Himself]</char>, the son of Yoyariv <char style="add">[Yehovah contends]</char>, the son of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, the son of Shiloni <char style="add">[peace bringer]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />All the sons of Peretz <char style="add">[breach (breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)]</char> that dwelt at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace] [were]</char> four hundred threescore and eight valiant men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> the sons of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>; Salu <char style="add">[weighed]</char> the son of Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>, the son of Yo’ed <char style="add">[Yehovah is witness]</char>, the son of P’dayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has ransomed]</char>, the son of Kolayah <char style="add">[voice of Yehovah]</char>, the son of Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char>, the son of Iti’el <char style="add">[God is with me]</char>, the son of Yesha’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And after him Gabai <char style="add">[my back]</char>, Salai <char style="add">[weighted]</char>, nine hundred twenty and eight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Yo’el <char style="add">[Yehovah is God]</char> the son of Zikhri <char style="add">[Illustrious] [was]</char> their overseer: and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> the son of Senuah <char style="add">[was]</char> second over the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Of the priests: Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char> the son of Yoyariv <char style="add">[Yehovah contends]</char>, Yakhin <char style="add">[He will establish]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />S’rayah <char style="add">[Yehovah is ruler]</char> the son of Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, the son of Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>, the son of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>, the son of M’rayot <char style="add">[rebellious]</char>, the son of Achituv <char style="add">[my brother is good]</char>, <char style="add">[was]</char> the ruler of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And their brethren that did the work of the house <char style="add">[were]</char> eight hundred twenty and two: and ‘Adayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has adorned Himself]</char> the son of Yerocham <char style="add">[showing pity]</char>, the son of P’lalyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, the son of Amtzi <char style="add">[my strength]</char>, the son of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, the son of Pash’chur <char style="add">[freedom]</char>, the son of Malkiyah <char style="add">[my king is Yehovah]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And his brethren, chief of the fathers, two hundred forty and two: and ‘Amash’sai <char style="add">[burdensome]</char> the son of ‘Azar’el <char style="add">[God has helped]</char>, the son of Achzai <char style="add">[my holder, protector]</char>, the son of Meshillemot <char style="add">[recompense]</char>, the son of Immer <char style="add">[he has said]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And their brethren, mighty men of valour, an hundred twenty and eight: and their overseer <char style="add">[was]</char> Zavdi’el <char style="add">[God is my endowment]</char>, the son of <char style="add">[one of]</char> the great men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Also of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the son of Hashuv <char style="add">[considerate]</char>, the son of ‘Azrikam <char style="add">[help against the enemy]</char>, the son of Hashavyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char>, the son of Buni <char style="add">[built]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Shabtai <char style="add">[sabbatical]</char> and Yozavad <char style="add">[Yehovah has endowed]</char>, of the chief of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, <char style="add">[had]</char> the oversight of the outward business of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char> the son of Mikha <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, the son of Zavdi <char style="add">[Endowment]</char>, the son of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>, <char style="add">[was]</char> the principal to begin the thanksgiving in prayer: and Bakbukyah <char style="add">[wasting of Yehovah]</char> the second among his brethren, and ‘Avda <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char> the son of Shamua <char style="add">[Renowned]</char>, the son of Galal <char style="add">[influential]</char>, the son of Y’dutun <char style="add">[praising]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />All the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> in the holy city <char style="add">[were]</char> two hundred eighty and four.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Moreover the porters, ‘Akuv <char style="add">[insidious]</char>, Talmon <char style="add">[oppressor]</char>, and their brethren that kept the gates, <char style="add">[were]</char> an hundred seventy and two.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, of the priests, <char style="add">[and]</char> the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> in all the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, everyone in his inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But the temple servants dwelt in ‘Ofel <char style="add">[hill]</char>: and Tzicha <char style="add">[parched]</char> and Gishpa <char style="add">[caress] [were]</char> over the temple servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />The overseer also of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace] [was]</char> ‘Uzi <char style="add">[strong]</char> the son of Bani <char style="add">[built]</char>, the son of Hashavyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char>, the son of Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>, the son of Mikha <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>. Of the sons of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>, the singers <char style="add">[were]</char> over the business of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For <char style="add">[it was]</char> the king’s commandment concerning them, that a certain portion should be for the singers, due for every day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And P’tachyah <char style="add">[freed by Yehovah]</char> the son of Mesheizav’el <char style="add">[God delivers]</char>, of the children of Zerach <char style="add">[Rising]</char> the son of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, <char style="add">[was]</char> at the king’s hand in all matters concerning the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And for the villages, with their fields, <char style="add">[some]</char> of the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> dwelt at Kiryat-Arba <char style="add">[City of Arba (four)]</char>, and <char style="add">[in]</char> the villages thereof, and at Divon <char style="add">[Wasting]</char>, and <char style="add">[in]</char> the villages thereof, and at Y’kabze’el <char style="add">[God gathers]</char>, and <char style="add">[in]</char> the villages thereof,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And at Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, and at Moladah <char style="add">[Birth or Race]</char>, and at Beit-Pelet <char style="add">[house of escape]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And at Hatzar-Shu’al <char style="add">[Jackal Village]</char>, and at Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>, and <char style="add">[in]</char> the villages thereof,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And at Ziklag <char style="add">[Winding]</char>, and at M’khonah <char style="add">[foundation]</char>, and in the villages thereof,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And at ‘Ein-Rimmon <char style="add">[fount of the pomegranate]</char>, and at Tzar’ah <char style="add">[hornet]</char>, and at Yarmut <char style="add">[Heights]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Zanoach <char style="add">[Cast Off]</char>, ‘Adulam <char style="add">[Justice of the People]</char>, and <char style="add">[in]</char> their villages, at Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char>, and the fields thereof, at ‘Azekah <char style="add">[Dug Over]</char>, and <char style="add">[in]</char> the villages thereof. And they dwelt from Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char> unto the valley of Hinnom <char style="add">[Lamentation]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />The children also of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> from Geva <char style="add">[hill] [dwelt]</char> at Mikhmas <char style="add">[hidden]</char>, and ‘Ayah <char style="add">[heap of ruins]</char>, and Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and <char style="add">[in]</char> their villages,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> at ‘Anatot <char style="add">[answers to prayer]</char>, Nov <char style="add">[high place]</char>, ‘Ananyah <char style="add">[Yehovah clouds]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Hatzor <char style="add">[Castle]</char>, Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, Gittayim <char style="add">[two winepresses]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Hadid <char style="add">[sharp]</char>, Tzvoyim <char style="add">[Gazelles]</char>, N’valat <char style="add">[hidden folly]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Lod <char style="add">[travail]</char>, and Ono <char style="add">[vigorous]</char>, the valley of craftsmen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [were]</char> divisions <char style="add">[in]</char> Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> in Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that went up with Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char> the son of Sh’alti’el <char style="add">[I have asked of God]</char>, and Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>: S’rayah <char style="add">[Yehovah is ruler]</char>, Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char>, ‘Ezra,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Amaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah speaks]</char>, Malukh <char style="add">[counselor]</char>, Hatush <char style="add">[assembled]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Sh’khanyah <char style="add">[dweller with Yehovah]</char>, Rechum <char style="add">[compassion]</char>, M’remot <char style="add">[elevations]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness]</char>, Gintoi <char style="add">[gardener]</char>, Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Miyamin <char style="add">[from the right hand]</char>, Ma’adiyah <char style="add">[adorned of Yah]</char>, Bilgah <char style="add">[cheerfulness]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, and Yoyariv <char style="add">[Yehovah contends]</char>, Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Salu <char style="add">[weighed]</char>, ‘Amok <char style="add">[to be deep]</char>, Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char>. These <char style="add">[were]</char> the chief of the priests and of their brethren in the days of Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Moreover the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, Binui <char style="add">[built up]</char>, Kadmi’el <char style="add">[God is the ancient one]</char>, Sherevyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has scorched]</char>, Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>, <char style="add">[which was]</char> over the thanksgiving, he and his brethren.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Also Bakbukyah <char style="add">[wasting of Yehovah]</char> and ‘Uni <char style="add">[afflicted]</char>, their brethren, <char style="add">[were]</char> over against them in the watches.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Yoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char>, Yoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char> also begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char>, and Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Yoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Yoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> Yadua <char style="add">[knowing]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And in the days of Yoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char> were priests, the chief of the fathers: of S’rayah <char style="add">[Yehovah is ruler]</char>, M’rayah <char style="add">[rebellion]</char>; of Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char>, Hananyah <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Of ‘Ezra, Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>; of Amaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah speaks]</char>, Y’hochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Of M’likhu <char style="add">[counselor]</char>, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>; of Sh’vanyah <char style="add">[increased by Yehovah]</char>, Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Of Harim <char style="add">[dedicated]</char>, ‘Adna <char style="add">[rest, or pleasure]</char>; of M’rayot <char style="add">[rebellious]</char>, Helkai <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Of ‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness]</char>, Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>; of Ginton <char style="add">[gardener]</char>, Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Of Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>, Zikhri <char style="add">[Illustrious]</char>; of Minyamin <char style="add">[from the right hand]</char>, of Mo’adyah <char style="add">[the set tome of Yah]</char>, Piltai <char style="add">[my deliverances]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Of Bilgah <char style="add">[cheerfulness]</char>, Shamua <char style="add">[Renowned]</char>; of Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has given]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And of Yoyariv <char style="add">[Yehovah contends]</char>, Matnai <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>; of Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char>, ‘Uzi <char style="add">[strong]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Of Salai <char style="add">[weighted]</char>, Kallai <char style="add">[swift]</char>; of ‘Amok <char style="add">[to be deep]</char>, ‘Ever <char style="add">[The Region Beyond]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Of Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, Hashavyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char>; of Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char>, N’tan’el <char style="add">[God’s Gift]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />The Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> in the days of Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char>, Yoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, and Yochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char>, and Yadua <char style="add">[knowing]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> recorded chief of the fathers: also the priests, to the reign of Daryavesh <char style="pn">(Darius)</char> <char style="add">[lord]</char> the Persian.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />The sons of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>, the chief of the fathers, <char style="add">[were]</char> written in the book of the chronicles, even until the days of Yochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char> the son of Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the chief of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: Hashavyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char>, Sherevyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has scorched]</char>, and Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char> the son of Kadmi’el <char style="add">[God is the ancient one]</char>, with their brethren over against them, to praise <char style="add">[and]</char> to give thanks, according to the commandment of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> over against ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>, and Bakbukyah <char style="add">[wasting of Yehovah]</char>, ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>, Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>, Talmon <char style="add">[oppressor]</char>, ‘Akuv <char style="add">[insidious]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> porters keeping the ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> at the thresholds of the gates.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />These <char style="add">[were]</char> in the days of Yoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char> the son of Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, the son of Yotzadak <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, and in the days of Nechemyah <char style="add">[God comforts]</char> the governor, and of ‘the priest, the scribe.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And at the dedication of the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> they sought the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> out of all their places, to bring them to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to keep the dedication with gladness, both with thanksgivings, and with singing, <char style="add">[with]</char> cymbals, psalteries, and with harps.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the sons of the singers gathered themselves together, both out of the plain country round about Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and from the villages of N’tofati <char style="add">[dropping]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Also from the house of Gilgal <char style="add">[A Wheel, Rolling]</char>, and out of the fields of Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char> and ‘Azmavet <char style="add">[strong unto death]</char>: for the singers had built them villages round about Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> purified themselves, and purified the people, and the gates, and the wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then I brought up the princes of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> upon the wall, and appointed two great <char style="add">[companies of them that gave]</char> thanks, <char style="add">[whereof one]</char> went on the right hand upon the wall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> the dung gate:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And after them went Hosha’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah as saved]</char>, and half of the princes of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, ‘Ezra, and Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, and Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And <char style="add">[certain]</char> of the priests’ sons with trumpets; <char style="add">[namely]</char>, Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char> the son of Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char>, the son of Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, the son of Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>, the son of Mikhayah <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, the son of Zakur <char style="add">[Mindful]</char>, the son of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And his brethren, Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, and ‘Azar’el <char style="add">[God has helped]</char>, Milalai <char style="add">[eloquent]</char>, Gilalai <char style="add">[weighty]</char>, Ma’ai <char style="add">[compassionate]</char>, N’tan’el <char style="add">[God’s Gift]</char>, and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char>, with the musical instruments of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and ‘the scribe before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And at the fountain gate, which was over against them, they went up by the stairs of the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, at the going up of the wall, above the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, even unto the water gate eastward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the other <char style="add">[company of them that gave]</char> thanks went over against <char style="add">[them]</char>, and I after them, and the half of the people upon the wall, from beyond the tower of the furnaces even unto the broad wall;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And from above the gate of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and above the old gate, and above the fish gate, and the tower of Hanan’el <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char>, and the tower of Me’ah <char style="add">[hundred]</char>, even unto the sheep gate: and they stood still in the prison gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />So stood the two <char style="add">[companies of them that gave]</char> thanks in the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and I, and the half of the rulers with me:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And the priests; Elyakim <char style="add">[God sets up]</char>, Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char>, Minyamin <char style="add">[from the right hand]</char>, Mikhayah <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, Elyo’eina <char style="add">[unto Yehovah are my eyes]</char>, Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> Hananyah <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char>, with trumpets;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char>, and Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, and El’azar <char style="add">[God has helped]</char>, and ‘Uzi <char style="add">[strong]</char>, and Y’hochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char>, and Malkiyah <char style="add">[my king is Yehovah]</char>, and ‘Eilam <char style="add">[eternity]</char>, and ‘Ezer <char style="add">[treasure]</char>. And the singers sang loud, with Yizarchyah <char style="add">[Yehovah will shine] [their]</char> overseer.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />Also that day they offered great sacrifices, and rejoiced: for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had made them rejoice with great joy: the wives also and the children rejoiced: so that the joy of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> was heard even afar off.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And at that time were some appointed over the chambers for the treasures, for the offerings, for the firstfruits, and for the tithes, to gather into them out of the fields of the cities the portions of the law for the priests and Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: for Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> rejoiced for the priests and for the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that waited.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And both the singers and the porters kept the ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> of their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and the ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> of the purification, according to the commandment of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />For in the days of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char> of old <char style="add">[there were]</char> chief of the singers, and songs of praise and thanksgiving unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />And all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in the days of Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char>, and in the days of Nechemyah <char style="add">[God comforts]</char>, gave the portions of the singers and the porters, every day his portion: and they sanctified <char style="add">[holy things]</char> unto the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>; and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> sanctified <char style="add">[them]</char> unto the children of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />On that day they read in the book of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> in the audience of the people; and in it was found written, that the ‘Amoni <char style="add">[tribal]</char> and the Mo’avi <char style="add">[from father: what father?]</char> should not come into the congregation of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> forever;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Because they met not the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with bread and with water, but hired Bil’am <char style="add">[Not of the People]</char> against them, that he should curse them: howbeit our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> turned the curse into a blessing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now it came to pass, when they had heard the law, that they separated from Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> all the mixed multitude.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And before this, Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char> the priest, having the oversight of the chamber of the house of our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[was]</char> allied unto Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he had prepared for him a great chamber, where aforetime they laid the meat offerings, the frankincense, and the vessels, and the tithes of the corn, the New Wine, and the oil, which was commanded <char style="add">[to be given]</char> to the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and the singers, and the porters; and the offerings of the priests.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But in all this <char style="add">[time]</char> was not I at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: for in the two and thirtieth year of Artach’shashta <char style="add">[I will make the spoiled to boil: I will stir myself (in) winter]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> came I unto the king, and after certain days obtained I leave of the king:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and understood of the evil that Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char> did for Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, in preparing him a chamber in the courts of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it grieved me sore: therefore I cast forth all the household stuff of Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char> out of the chamber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then I commanded, and they cleansed the chambers: and there brought I again the vessels of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, with the meat offering and the frankincense.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And I perceived that the portions of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> had not been given <char style="add">[them]</char>: for the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> and the singers, that did the work, were fled everyone to his field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then contended I with the rulers, and said, Why is the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> forsaken? And I gathered them together, and set them in their place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then brought all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> the tithe of the corn and the New Wine and the oil unto the treasuries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I made treasurers over the treasuries, Shelemyah <char style="add">[repaid by Yehovah] [repaid by Yehovah]</char> the priest, and Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the scribe, and of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, P’dayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has ransomed]</char>: and next to them <char style="add">[was]</char> Hanan <char style="add">[he is merciful]</char> the son of Zakur <char style="add">[Mindful]</char>, the son of Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>: for they were counted faithful, and their office <char style="add">[was]</char> to distribute unto their brethren.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Remember me, O my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, concerning this, and wipe not out my good deeds that I have done for the house of my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and for the offices thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />In those days saw I in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [some]</char> treading wine presses on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, and bringing in sheaves, and lading asses; as also wine, grapes, and figs, and all <char style="add">[manner of]</char> burdens, which they brought into Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day: and I testified <char style="add">[against them]</char> in the day wherein they sold victuals <char style="pn">(food for humans)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />There dwelt men of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyre)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> also in it, which brought fish, and all manner of ware, and sold on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> unto the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then I contended with the nobles of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and said unto them, What evil thing <char style="add">[is]</char> this that you<char style="ord">2f</char> do, and Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Did not your fathers thus, and did not our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> bring all this evil upon us, and upon this city? yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> bring more wrath upon Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by profaning the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And it came to pass, that when the gates of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> began to be dark before the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, I commanded that the gates should be shut, and charged that they should not be opened till after the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>: and <char style="add">[some]</char> of my servants set I at the gates, <char style="add">[that]</char> there should no burden be brought in on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />So the merchants and sellers of all kind of ware lodged without Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> once or twice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then I testified against them, and said unto them, Why lodge you<char style="ord">2f</char> about the wall? if you<char style="ord">2f</char> do <char style="add">[so]</char> again, I will lay hands on you. From that time forth came they no <char style="add">[more]</char> on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And I commanded the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that they should cleanse themselves, and <char style="add">[that]</char> they should come <char style="add">[and]</char> keep the gates, to sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use) the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day. Remember me, O my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[concerning]</char> this also, and spare me according to the greatness of you<char style="ord">i</char> mercy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />In those days also saw I Y’hudim <char style="pn">(Judeans)</char> <char style="add">[that]</char> had married wives of Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And their children spoke half in the speech of Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and could not speak in the Y’hudit <char style="pn">(Y’hudim (Judeans))</char> language, but according to the language of each people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And I contended with them, and cursed them, and struck certain of them, and plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not give your daughters unto their sons, nor take their daughters unto your sons, or for yourselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Did not Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sin by these things? yet among many nations was there no king like him, who was beloved of his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> made him king over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: nevertheless even him did outlandish women cause to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Shall we then hearken unto you to do all this great evil, to transgress against our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in marrying strange wives?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And <char style="add">[one]</char> of the sons of Yoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, the son of Elyashiv <char style="add">[God restores]</char> the High Priest, <char style="add">[was]</char> son in law to Sanvalat <char style="add">[strength]</char> the Horoni <char style="add">[native of twin caves]</char>: therefore I chased him from me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Remember them, O my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, because they have defiled the priesthood, and the covenant of the priesthood, and of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Thus cleansed I them from all strangers, and appointed the wards of the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, everyone in his business;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And for the wood offering, at times appointed, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, for good.</para>
</usx>